    "b-shape-ref-intro-1": {
      "id": "b-shape-ref-intro-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A per-shape visual and connection reference: every one of the 11 InteractiveCanvasObjectType values at its default creation geometry, with its real computed connection-anchor positions and its text-slot behavior, each illustrated by a live canvas embed. This bundle builds on the model layer's field-by-field object type reference in canvas-10-model — schema fields and validation rules are documented there, not repeated here — and on the shape API design doc canvas-10-system-design-10-shape-api. What this reference adds is the connection-facing view: where connectors actually attach on each shape, and where each shape puts its text."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-shape-ref-intro-2": {
      "id": "b-shape-ref-intro-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Anchor resolution in one breath: getConnectionAnchors (in objects/geometry.ts since the P3 geometry move) builds four cardinal candidates offset ANCHOR_OFFSET_PX (10 world px) outside the object's bound, then projects each along the ray from the object's center onto the shape's real outline via outlinePolygon. Outlines are def-declared OutlineSpecs now: true outlines cover pill, diamond, arrow-shape, ellipse, and the polygon set (triangle, octagon); every other type falls back to its axis-aligned bounding rect. During an interactive connect, resolveConnectionCascade snaps the pointer to the nearest cardinal anchor within ANCHOR_SNAP_VIEW_PX (8 view px, divided by zoom), else to the nearest outline point within OUTLINE_SNAP_WORLD_PX (8 world px), else connects to the shape's center when the pointer is inside it, else falls through to a free point."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-shape-ref-intro-3": {
      "id": "b-shape-ref-intro-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Every embed below follows the same recipe: the subject shape sits at its "
        },
        {
          "insert": "OBJECT_TYPE_DEFAULTS",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas/src/state/schema/object-defaults.ts",
              "symbol": "OBJECT_TYPE_DEFAULTS"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " creation size, with four small "
        },
        {
          "insert": "text",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " (caption) markers outside it. Each marker's connection endpoint stores BOTH the coarse side anchor and the exact "
        },
        {
          "insert": "position",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " "
        },
        {
          "insert": "[rx, ry]",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " that "
        },
        {
          "insert": "getConnectionAnchors",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas/src/objects/geometry.ts",
              "symbol": "getConnectionAnchors"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " computes for that side — so the rendered connector lands on the true outline anchor, not a hand-guessed point. On most shapes those four points coincide with the bounds-edge midpoints; on "
        },
        {
          "insert": "arrow-shape",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " the top/bottom anchors sit visibly inside the bounding box, on the chevron body's edges. A fifth free-floating caption under each shape states the text-slot rule (centered vs. top-left vs. below-icon vs. body-only)."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
